#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0072fd14-c312-5229-9ffa-9b46c1ecd180" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Regression Line Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "15c6c8c2-9c56-5eff-bfc6-36cfe174ee3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9715" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$9$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $6$ | $4$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nConsider the data sets above. You are given that $\\overline{x}=4$ and $\\overline{y}=3.$ Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line. Round the slope and the $y$-intercept to $1$ decimal place if necessary." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny = mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m{:}$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(1-4)(6-3)+(2-4)(4-3) \\\\  & +(4-4)(2-3)+(9-4)(0-3) \\\\  & =(-3)(3)+(-2)(1)+(0)(-1)+(5)(-3) \\\\  & =-9-2-0-15 \\\\  & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(1-4)^{2}+(2-4)^{2}+(4-4)^{2}+(9-4)^{2} \\\\  & =9+4+0+25 \\\\  & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm = \\dfrac{-26}{38} = -\\dfrac{13}{19} \\approx -0.7.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =3-(-\\frac{13}{19})\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{109}{19} \\\\  & ≈5.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny = -0.7x + 5.7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f904b9b7-b565-5bee-8f6f-c319a7cb9d7b" :knowledge-point/title "Making Predictions by Calculating a Regression Line"}] :question/id #uuid "9c9247a2-0a43-5dec-b477-bb60f8f57c0d" :question/math-academy-id "e-9716" :question/problem "| **Years ($x$)** | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Value ($y$)** | **$35$** | **$26$** | **$19$** | **$16$** |\n\nThe table above gives the value of a car a few years after it was purchased (in thousands of dollars). You are given that $\\overline{x}=2$ and $\\overline{y}=24.$ Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line and use this to predict how long it takes for the car's value to drop to $\\[math]10\\,000.$ Round your answer to the nearest year." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny = mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m{:}$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(0-2)(35-24)+(1-2)(26-24) \\\\  & +(3-2)(19-24)+(4-2)(16-24) \\\\  & =(-2)(11)+(-1)(2)+(1)(-5)+(2)(-8) \\\\  & =-22-2-5-16 \\\\  & =-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(0-2)^{2}+(1-2)^{2}+(3-2)^{2}+(4-2)^{2} \\\\  & =4+1+1+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Now, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm =-\\dfrac{45}{10} = -4.5.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =24-(-\\frac{9}{2})\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny = -4.5x+33\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate the required value by substituting $y=10$ into the equation of the trend line and solving for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4.5x+33 \\\\ 10 & =-4.5x+33 \\\\ -23 & =-4.5x \\\\ x & ≈5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, it takes approximately $5$ years for the car's value to drop to $\\[math]10\\,000.$\n\n**Note:** Since we're extrapolating (the point where $y=10$ is not within the original data range), our result *may* be unreliable."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f904b9b7-b565-5bee-8f6f-c319a7cb9d7b" :knowledge-point/title "Making Predictions by Calculating a Regression Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0336c168-4099-510b-a594-3b3934526e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552871} {:answer/id #uuid "1e747479-8878-5613-8c9c-88451ac3c939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "107.7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552923} {:answer/id #uuid "77d80668-ccd3-5a96-a0d9-977ec6a4f2a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108.6\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553111} {:answer/id #uuid "83678f4e-e4ae-526f-84f4-1a82f18c8a00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "109.0\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553133} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b789f3-1f71-5341-be9a-36e79910b938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "107.9\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83678f4e-e4ae-526f-84f4-1a82f18c8a00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "109.0\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553133} :answer-field/id #uuid "67250215-1e03-538c-9563-cca87464372b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8d3e7fb-7b7e-5708-a3c3-52c0d9f411c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134208" :question/problem "| **Age ($x$)** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$9$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Height ($y$)** | $95$ | $106$ | $110$ | $125$ |\n\nThe table above gives the ages, in years, and the corresponding heights, in centimeters, of Milly and Rasheed's four children. You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=109.$ \n\nFind the equation of the corresponding linear regression line and use this to predict the children's height when they are $6$ years old. Round the regression line's coefficients to three decimal places and your final answer to the nearest tenth of a centimeter." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(3-6)(95-109)+(5-6)(106-109) \\\\  & +(7-6)(110-109)+(9-6)(125-109) \\\\  & =(-3)(-14)+(-1)(-3)+(1)(1)+(3)(16) \\\\  & =42+3+1+48 \\\\  & =94\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(3-6)^{2}+(5-6)^{2}+(7-6)^{2}+(9-6)^{2} \\\\  & =9+1+1+9 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{94}{20}=\\frac{47}{10}=4.7.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =109-4.7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =109-28.2 \\\\  & =80.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=4.7x+80.8.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can predict the height of a six-year-old child in this family by substituting $x=6$ into our regression line:\n\n$$\ny=4.7(6)+80.8=109\n$$\n\nTherefore, the model predicts that a six-year-old child will be $109.0\\,\\text{cm}$ tall."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0072fd14-c312-5229-9ffa-9b46c1ecd180" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Regression Line Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37cbb3fd-73e5-5e8d-9690-8763071dfd32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1.6x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552978} {:answer/id #uuid "45a9f338-b92d-5726-b985-633b4a3fbffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2.1x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553010} {:answer/id #uuid "4e825e05-cf1d-521e-8e48-f222ef8fea1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-7x+1.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553040} {:answer/id #uuid "d0486f24-94ec-5707-918c-3131894abe26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1.2x+6.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553286} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6e8408-98d8-5ae0-8d49-775c9ff55469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef6e8408-98d8-5ae0-8d49-775c9ff55469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553342} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5b4ca26-bcc7-56b7-afb9-4a67fc3172f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22d42a89-d817-5352-921e-6f3ec86ac62f" :question/math-academy-id "q-134521" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $7$ | $5$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nConsider the data sets above. You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=2$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=3.$ Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line. Round the slope and the $y$-intercept to $1$ decimal place if necessary." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(0-2)(7-3)+(1-2)(5-3) \\\\  & +(3-2)(1-3)+(4-2)(-1-3) \\\\  & =(-2)(4)+(-1)(2)+(1)(-2)+(2)(-4) \\\\  & =-8-2-2-8 \\\\  & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(0-2)^{2}+(1-2)^{2}+(3-2)^{2}+(4-2)^{2} \\\\  & =4+1+1+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{-20}{10}=-2.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =3-(-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3+4 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=-2x+7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f904b9b7-b565-5bee-8f6f-c319a7cb9d7b" :knowledge-point/title "Making Predictions by Calculating a Regression Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cd4c0fb-caf1-5f4f-a432-bb5fd3ff247b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$78$ points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552882} {:answer/id #uuid "67c6c97a-0bb6-501a-b7cc-76baa2095830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$80$ points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553086} {:answer/id #uuid "b64589e6-c3b6-5a58-adf0-488fce7b8549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$77$ points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553231} {:answer/id #uuid "d29d6acc-aa34-5c55-b6c6-cf266929ebe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$79$ points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553288} {:answer/id #uuid "de19434b-df45-5944-bc31-db1c8b80ded8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$82$ points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67c6c97a-0bb6-501a-b7cc-76baa2095830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$80$ points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553086} :answer-field/id #uuid "64e44a62-8213-5c6f-80df-59eef2307e74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cc8754de-7209-53e4-a8f7-9e3f115b2f92" :question/math-academy-id "q-134589" :question/problem "| **Study Hours ($x$)** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$1$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Average Grade ($y$)** | $71$ | $75$ | $65$ | $85$ |\n\nThe table above gives the number of study hours per day and the corresponding average grades (in points) of four students. You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=2$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=74.$ \n\nFind the equation of the corresponding linear regression line and use this to predict the average grade for a student that studies $3$ hours per day. Round the regression line's coefficients to three decimal places and your final answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(1-2)(71-74)+(2-2)(75-74) \\\\  & +(1-2)(65-74)+(4-2)(85-74) \\\\  & =(-1)(-3)+(0)(1)+(-1)(-9)+(2)(11) \\\\  & =3+0+9+22 \\\\  & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(1-2)^{2}+(2-2)^{2}+(1-2)^{2}+(4-2)^{2} \\\\  & =1+0+1+4 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{34}{6}=\\frac{17}{3}≈5.667.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =74-\\frac{17}{3}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{188}{3} \\\\  & ≈62.667\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=5.667x+62.667.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can predict the average grade of a student that studies $3$ hours per day by substituting $x=3$ into our regression line:\n\n$$\ny=5.667(3)+62.667≈80\n$$\n\nTherefore, the model predicts that a student that studies three hours per day will have an average grade of $80$ points."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f904b9b7-b565-5bee-8f6f-c319a7cb9d7b" :knowledge-point/title "Making Predictions by Calculating a Regression Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28a0a6b5-fa56-5177-8252-49d5bec965c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7.2$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552941} {:answer/id #uuid "54cc76a5-4452-5793-ba72-32f997a468b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6.1$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553051} {:answer/id #uuid "5717c494-07c0-5e56-a9d7-736aef722a2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3.5$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553055} {:answer/id #uuid "b8bfc69b-143f-5630-830c-5683834f3ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4.2$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553236} {:answer/id #uuid "e6cb6aa0-e154-57b0-8bed-8664f4ac1273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2.9$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8bfc69b-143f-5630-830c-5683834f3ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4.2$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553236} :answer-field/id #uuid "52ec2b83-6910-5f4f-81eb-01603d3d75bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "92e8138f-b7f0-50e4-b13c-66a8af5c74ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-134594" :question/problem "| **Weight $(kg)$ of Apples ($x$)** | **$30$** | **$44$** | **$50$** | **$52$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Hours ($y$)** | $5$ | $6$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n\nA farmer wants to understand the relation between the weight of apples to harvest and the time needed to do the job.\nThe table above gives the weight of apples harvested and the corresponding number of work hours over a sample of four days. You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=44$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=6.$ \n\nFind the equation of the corresponding linear regression line and use this to predict the time needed when there are $20$ kilograms of apples to collect. Round the regression line's coefficients to three decimal places and your final answer to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(30-44)(5-6)+(44-44)(6-6) \\\\  & +(50-44)(6-6)+(52-44)(7-6) \\\\  & =(-14)(-1)+(0)(0)+(6)(0)+(8)(1) \\\\  & =14+0+0+8 \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(30-44)^{2}+(44-44)^{2}+(50-44)^{2}+(52-44)^{2} \\\\  & =196+0+36+64 \\\\  & =296\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{22}{296}=\\frac{11}{148}≈0.074.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =6-\\frac{11}{148}\\cdot 44 \\\\  & ≈2.730\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=0.074x+2.730.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can predict the time needed to harvest $20$ kilograms by substituting $x=20$ into our regression line:\n\n$$\ny=0.074(20)+2.730≈4.2\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, it takes $4.2$ hours to harvest $20\\,\\text{kg}$ of apples.\n\nNote: Since we're extrapolating (the point where $x=20$ is not within the original data range), our result *may* be unreliable."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f904b9b7-b565-5bee-8f6f-c319a7cb9d7b" :knowledge-point/title "Making Predictions by Calculating a Regression Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fec5b9d-5c17-5896-a796-e52b199c8b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4.5$ weeks" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552998} {:answer/id #uuid "600b6b62-22db-55a2-aed2-2737121eeef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3.7$ weeks" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553073} {:answer/id #uuid "85ac7239-5b0a-5fb9-8dc3-9f474530606a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4.0$ weeks" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553136} {:answer/id #uuid "960d12df-8477-50bd-a1a0-3fd5f8923d11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3.2$ weeks" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553175} {:answer/id #uuid "e0690624-5ae0-5d48-bbe6-681f08580e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3.4$ weeks" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "600b6b62-22db-55a2-aed2-2737121eeef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3.7$ weeks" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553073} :answer-field/id #uuid "2db85191-362a-53e4-8530-d74c2a65384d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f0e8a005-d5ef-567f-838c-cadbb31dd290" :question/math-academy-id "q-134604" :question/problem "| **Weeks ($x$)** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$7$** | **$8$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Increase in Words per Minute ($y$)** | $20$ | $44$ | $102$ | $118$ |\n\nThe instructor of a $10$-week speed reading course monitors the students' progress during the course.\nThe table above gives the number of weeks of attendance and the corresponding increase in the number of words per minute for four students. You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=5$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=71.$ \n\nFind the equation of the corresponding linear regression line and use this to predict how many weeks are needed to see an increase of $50$ words per minute. Round the regression line's coefficients to three decimal places and your final answer to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(2-5)(20-71)+(3-5)(44-71) \\\\  & +(7-5)(102-71)+(8-5)(118-71) \\\\  & =(-3)(-51)+(-2)(-27)+(2)(31)+(3)(47) \\\\  & =153+54+62+141 \\\\  & =410\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(2-5)^{2}+(3-5)^{2}+(7-5)^{2}+(8-5)^{2} \\\\  & =9+4+4+9 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{410}{26}=\\frac{205}{13}≈15.769.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =71-\\frac{205}{13}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-7.846\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=15.769x-7.846\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate the required value by substituting $y=50$ into the equation of the trend line and solving for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =15.769x-7.846 \\\\ 50 & =15.769x-7.846 \\\\ 57.846 & =15.769x \\\\ x & ≈3.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, students have an increase of $50$ words per minute after approximately $3.7$ weeks."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f904b9b7-b565-5bee-8f6f-c319a7cb9d7b" :knowledge-point/title "Making Predictions by Calculating a Regression Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae54c441-d47e-508c-8999-640555d0f079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553220} {:answer/id #uuid "cd85d822-b458-5afc-8f82-96c68776f968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553280} {:answer/id #uuid "d3873d28-7cf2-58e7-b49f-e9b7810ef93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553291} {:answer/id #uuid "e1602e5e-50f0-5e4f-810a-60fa0c496f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553318} {:answer/id #uuid "f67e0a68-39cc-5086-b355-1dee00b5c62c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3873d28-7cf2-58e7-b49f-e9b7810ef93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553291} :answer-field/id #uuid "f216e67f-ab1c-5fee-9211-3c0531cfbf93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8625effc-a6bf-5c01-9019-062227a65c85" :question/math-academy-id "q-134605" :question/problem "| **Years ($x$)** | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Value ($y$)** | **$20$** | **$18$** | **$15$** | **$11$** |\n\nThe table above gives the value of a motorcycle a few years after it was purchased (in thousands of dollars). You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=2$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=16.$ Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line and use this to predict how long it takes for the motorcycle to have a value of $$8\\,000.$ Round the answer to the nearest year." :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(0-2)(20-16)+(1-2)(18-16) \\\\  & +(3-2)(15-16)+(4-2)(11-16) \\\\  & =(-2)(4)+(-1)(2)+(1)(-1)+(2)(-5) \\\\  & =-8-2-1-10 \\\\  & =-21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(0-2)^{2}+(1-2)^{2}+(3-2)^{2}+(4-2)^{2} \\\\  & =4+1+1+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=-\\frac{21}{10}=-2.1.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =16-(-2.1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =20.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=-2.1x+20.2\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate the required value by substituting $y=8$ into the equation of the trend line and solving for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2.1x+20.2 \\\\ 8 & =-2.1x+20.2 \\\\ -12.2 & =-2.1x \\\\ x & ≈6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, it takes $6$ years for the motorcycle to have a value of $$8\\,000.$\n\nNote: Since we're extrapolating (the point where $y=8$ is not within the original data range), our result *may* be unreliable."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0072fd14-c312-5229-9ffa-9b46c1ecd180" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Regression Line Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "791002ae-cba4-5b34-b056-911cb05bc44f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "791002ae-cba4-5b34-b056-911cb05bc44f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553115} :answer-field/id #uuid "60c66de8-8a06-5e33-9364-15eccab96587" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba58e3f6-198c-5bbf-9cbe-3fc18f85dcf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-316324" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $8$ | $6$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nConsider the data sets above. You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=3$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=4.$ Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line. Round the slope and the $y$-intercept to **one decimal place** if necessary.\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(1-3)(8-4)+(2-3)(6-4) \\\\  & +(4-3)(2-4)+(5-3)(0-4) \\\\  & =(-2)(4)+(-1)(2)+(1)(-2)+(2)(-4) \\\\  & =-8-2-2-8 \\\\  & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(1-3)^{2}+(2-3)^{2}+(4-3)^{2}+(5-3)^{2} \\\\  & =4+1+1+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{-20}{10}=-2.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =4-(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4+6 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=-2x+10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0072fd14-c312-5229-9ffa-9b46c1ecd180" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Regression Line Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22c4dfcb-2d0e-5a9f-8507-74b8f3ae0fd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22c4dfcb-2d0e-5a9f-8507-74b8f3ae0fd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552930} :answer-field/id #uuid "46bfb3c5-83b3-5784-86ce-70ba204b4fe5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0355e885-ef6c-5de8-9a07-0844e006115f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316326" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$8$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nConsider the data sets above. You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=5$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=4.$ Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line. Round the slope and the $y$-intercept to **one decimal place** if necessary.\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(2-5)(7-4)+(4-5)(5-4) \\\\  & +(6-5)(3-4)+(8-5)(1-4) \\\\  & =(-3)(3)+(-1)(1)+(1)(-1)+(3)(-3) \\\\  & =-9-1-1-9 \\\\  & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(2-5)^{2}+(4-5)^{2}+(6-5)^{2}+(8-5)^{2} \\\\  & =9+1+1+9 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{-20}{20}=-1.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =4-(-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =4+5 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=-x+9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0072fd14-c312-5229-9ffa-9b46c1ecd180" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Regression Line Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7728b714-38ce-5255-ba9b-5fb24668a983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7728b714-38ce-5255-ba9b-5fb24668a983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553109} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0540983-8578-5a3f-ada5-e134f4acb871" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54d4d3b8-d729-5c07-8ab5-e817b0ad3339" :question/math-academy-id "q-316581" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $9$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ |\n\nConsider the data sets above. You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=4$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=6.$ Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line. Round the slope and the $y$-intercept to **one decimal place** if necessary.\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(1-4)(9-6)+(3-4)(7-6) \\\\  & +(5-4)(5-6)+(7-4)(3-6) \\\\  & =(-3)(3)+(-1)(1)+(1)(-1)+(3)(-3) \\\\  & =-9-1-1-9 \\\\  & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(1-4)^{2}+(3-4)^{2}+(5-4)^{2}+(7-4)^{2} \\\\  & =9+1+1+9 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{-20}{20}=-1.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =6-(-1)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=-x+10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0072fd14-c312-5229-9ffa-9b46c1ecd180" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Regression Line Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a00ca04-f14c-58d5-9ab3-c8221bd600cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a00ca04-f14c-58d5-9ab3-c8221bd600cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553118} :answer-field/id #uuid "08d99b4e-ce04-5c53-b6e9-817819d842a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ecc1a3cc-0f10-56ce-838a-ad42d1b426c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-365430" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$9$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $13$ | $9$ | $5$ | $1$ |\n\nConsider the data sets above. You are given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=7.$ Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line. Round the slope and the $y$-intercept to **one decimal place** if necessary.\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(3-6)(13-7)+(5-6)(9-7) \\\\  & +(7-6)(5-7)+(9-6)(1-7) \\\\  & =(-3)(6)+(-1)(2)+(1)(-2)+(3)(-6) \\\\  & =-18-2-2-18 \\\\  & =-40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(3-6)^{2}+(5-6)^{2}+(7-6)^{2}+(9-6)^{2} \\\\  & =9+1+1+9 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{-40}{20}=-2.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =7-(-2)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =7+12 \\\\  & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=-2x+19.\n$$"}]}
